and the last remaining medal of honor  recipient from world war ii died last  week today it was announced that  herschel woody williams will lie in  honor inside the capitol building the  date and other details are to be  announced at a later date west virginian  woody williams died wednesday at age 98  he earned his medal of honor in the  battle of iwo jima at age 22. williams  was never one to take credit though  i've been in  the medal of honor society since 1947.  but most of them will say  it doesn't belong to me  i wear it in honor of those  who never got to come home  and sacrifice their life i walk in the  footprints of somebody else i was born  free because somebody gave his life  to make it possible for me to be born  free  after world war ii woody served in the  marine corps reserve and worked at the  v.a helping fellow veterans for decades  the huntington west virginia va medical  center was actually renamed in his honor  and there is something thematic and  consistent with world war ii veterans  and it is that completely selfless  nature of always deflecting credit and  putting it on others it's really a  beautiful thing i i notice it  in countless interviews we've heard with  veterans i noticed it with my own uncle  jack who served in world war ii they  always want to give praise to others  what an honor though and also to just  have it you know just to be announced  today just gives it a whole different  meaning yeah absolutely agree with that
 

